{"title":"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is written on the blackboard. The sum of its digits is calculated. Then the sum of the\ndigits of the result is calculated and so on until we have a single digit. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/5/8f58fa0ed70c80d40f7ca4e1a86774f19b31b9a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2014$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, what\nis this digit?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lemma: The sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05ae985270be773fec916ebd576093bab6307574.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\pmod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> represent the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We can prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3ae148bd1c6d7400fc4f1fcb9cfa3b9b513c1203.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) \\equiv n \\mod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" /> by expressing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a089f2e02c1aa4d78a765fc478e1563e3bf7ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{a_k a_{k-1} \\cdots a_1 a_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />s are digits in the decimal expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. By using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b235ff4d022d626efd07dab75e998e665647f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9|10^n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f5582a5f7871240777bdc4462cdf026b6cc858a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = a_n \\cdot 10^n + a_{n-1} \\cdot 10^{n-1} + \\cdots + a_1 \\cdot 10^1 + a_0 \\cdot 10^0 \\equiv a_n + a_{n-1} + \\cdots + a_1 + a_0 = s(n) \\pmod 9\\]\" width=\"672\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad1554e8bdcff0a55e4de19596e0fb37b9b4a634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) = n \\pmod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Since we repeatedly compute the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the value of each term will be congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05ae985270be773fec916ebd576093bab6307574.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\pmod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, we only need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa4f6d51d0c5857b4164ec5e0e2aa434730004d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq k \\leq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dd7280652c1975b26e550139c8745af363a5320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\equiv 5^{2014} \\pmod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" />. Using Euler's formula, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/8/4b85ef7f5c50bb1e0bf2b7ba63a58fcae53e8a88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{\\phi(9)} = 5^6 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"23\" />. Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40ecaae3dd894342e7676ac3d348d151d38b0a44.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{2014} = 5^{2010} \\cdot 5^4 = (5^6)^{335} \\cdot 5^4 \\equiv 5^4 = 625 \\equiv 4 \\pmod 9\\]\" width=\"437\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>So our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4c6c07150a0f6e56b0a6e198d1d19155dfe96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>- mako17\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II\">2014 UNM-PNM Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://mathcontest.unm.edu/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</t